pub const GUIDE: &str = "TailScout is a small native GTK/libadwaita desktop controller for Tailscale.\n\nMain controls:\nConnect/Disconnect — starts or stops your Tailscale connection.\nLock — grants this Linux user operator permission through Polkit, so normal actions do not need sudo.\nDownload — receives Taildrop files into a folder you choose.\nPerson icon — shows saved Tailscale accounts/tailnets, login, logout, and switch.\nExit node — routes normal internet traffic through another approved Tailscale device.\nDevices — click a device for owner, routes, endpoints, Taildrop, exit-node, and traffic details.\n\nDesign:\nReads status through LocalAPI when available, falls back to the version-matched tailscale CLI, and runs all blocking calls off the GTK main thread. No Electron, no background runtime, no password storage.";

pub const CLI_CHEATSHEET: &str = "Daily:\ntailscale status\ntailscale status --json\ntailscale up --timeout=30s\ntailscale down\ntailscale login --timeout=30s\ntailscale logout\n\nAccounts:\ntailscale switch --list --json\ntailscale switch <profile>\n\nPermissions:\nsudo tailscale set --operator=$USER\npkexec tailscale set --operator=$USER\n\nTaildrop:\ntailscale file cp <file> <device>:\ntailscale file get --conflict=rename <folder>\n\nExit nodes:\ntailscale exit-node list\ntailscale exit-node suggest\ntailscale set --exit-node=<device-or-ip>\ntailscale set --exit-node=\ntailscale set --advertise-exit-node=true\n\nDiagnostics:\ntailscale netcheck\ntailscale ping <host>\ntailscale bugreport\ntailscale version\n\nAdvanced features exposed by the CLI but intentionally not all front-and-center in TailScout yet:\nserve, funnel, cert, ssh, drive, lock, metrics, dns, whois, syspolicy, app connector routes.";
